 suite is green (18 passed, everything else is legitimately `it.todo` in other unimplemented features). Here's the refactoring report.\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- `computeItemsBasePremium`, `computeInsuranceSum`, `computeTypePremium`, `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM`, `ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUE`, `BLOCK_SIZE`, `BLOCK_PREMIUM` — all names precisely match their purpose and are validated by all 16 tests (per-type base premium with block discount; flat insurance sum by type, unaffected by block discount).\n- No renames needed — names already reveal intent clearly.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (`computeItemsBasePremium` for-loop version, the only candidate with visible complexity):\n```typescript\nexport const computeItemsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const countsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const { type } of items) {\n    countsByType.set(type, (countsByType.get(type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  let total = 0;\n  for (const [type, count] of countsByType) {\n    total += computeTypePremium(type, count);\n  }\n  return total;\n};\n```\n- Bindings: `items, countsByType, type` (loop1) + `total, type, count` (loop2) = 6\n- Invocations: `new Map()`, `.set()`, `.get()`, `computeTypePremium()` = 4 → mass 8\n- Loops: 2 (`for...of` x2) → mass 10\n- Assignments: `total += ...` = 1 → mass 6\n- Constants: `0` (in `?? 0` and initial `total = 0`) = 2\n\nTotal Mass = 2 + 6 + 8 + 10 + 6 = **32**\n\n**Refactoring Applied** — Rule 4 (Fewest Elements) + Rule 3 (No Duplication of imperative accumulation pattern):\nReplaced the second `for` loop + mutable `total` accumulator with `Array.from(map).reduce(...)`, removing an explicit mutable-state loop while keeping the counting `Map` build (still clearest way to tally occurrences).\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```typescript\nexport const computeItemsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const countsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const { type } of items) {\n    countsByType.set(type, (countsByType.get(type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return [...countsByType].reduce(\n    (total, [type, count]) => total + computeTypePremium(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n};\n```\n- Bindings: `items, countsByType, type` (loop) + `total, type, count` (reduce params) = 6\n- Invocations: `new Map()`, `.set()`, `.get()`, spread-to-array, `.reduce()`, `computeTypePremium()` = 5 → mass 10\n- Loops: 2 (`for...of` + `reduce`) → mass 10\n- Assignments: 0 (no mutable accumulator now)\n- Constants: `0` (`?? 0` and reduce seed) = 2\n\nTotal Mass = 2 + 6 + 10 + 10 + 0 = **28**\n\n**Mass Change**: 32 → 28 (Δ -4), driven entirely by eliminating the mutable `total` assignment (mass 6) at the cost of one extra invocation (spread + reduce vs plain loop, +2).\n\nConsidered but rejected:\n- Merging insurance-sum's flat `ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUE` lookup with `ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM` into one combined table — rejected per Rule 2: the two concepts (base premium with block discounts vs. flat insurance value) are conceptually distinct and currently have different key sets (moonstone isn't insured yet); merging would create false coupling and violate the instruction not to add untested behavior.\n- Extracting a shared \"count by type\" helper for reuse elsewhere — no duplication exists yet (only one call site), so per Rule 4 this would be premature abstraction.\n\n**Refactoring Complete**:\n- **Refactoring**: Replaced imperative loop/accumulator in `computeItemsBasePremium` with `reduce`, removing a mutable assignment.\n- **Mass Change**: 32 → 28 (Δ -4)\n- **Naming**: No changes needed — all names already reveal intent.\n- **Tests**: All 16 catalog tests passing (18/18 non-todo tests in full suite passing)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/catalog.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/catalog.ts\nPassing te