eRate(item), 0);\n\nexport const computeRawPolicyPremium = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  computeItemsBasePremium(items) + computeItemSurcharges(items);\n```\n- Bindings: 1 (`items` param) \n- Invocations: 3 (`computeItemsBasePremium`, `computeItemSurcharges`, implicit `+`) \n- Loop: 0 (now lives once, inside `computeItemSurcharges`) \n→ `computeRawPolicyPremium` mass drops to ~7; the reduce/loop mass (5) now exists exactly once in the whole module instead of being duplicated in two call sites' conceptual footprint.\n\n**Mass Change**: Duplicated surcharge-total knowledge (≈14 mass unit pattern present twice) → single shared helper (mass ≈13 total, present once). Net effect: lower total mass and, more importantly, a single source of truth for \"how item surcharges are totaled.\"\n\n**Tests**: All 9 passing tests remain green (verified via `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test quote`).\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted duplicated item-surcharge-summation reduce into a new `computeItemSurcharges` helper, used by both `computeRawPolicyPremium` and `computeQuotePremium` (Rule 3 — No Duplication).\n**Mass Change**: Duplicated loop logic (in 2 places) → single shared loop (1 place); net reduction in total mass and improved single-source-of-truth for surcharge calculation.\n**Tests**: All passing (9 passed, 1 todo)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/quote.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/quote.ts\nPassing tests: 9\nRecent Green phase: Fixed a semantic bug -- the first-insurance surcharge (10% of policy base premium) now applies unconditionally to every quote (per the spec's integration example: \"each item in a quote is treated as a first insurance, regardless of customer history\"). The boolean parameter was renamed fr