LLOW_UP_CONTRACT_DISCOUNT_RATE;\n  return (\n    roundPremium(raw + firstInsuranceSurcharge - loyaltyDiscount - followUpContractDiscount) + PROCESSING_FEE\n  );\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784914254932},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Refactoring Report\n\n**Naming Evaluation** (first priority):\n- `computeQuotePremium`, `computeRawPolicyPremium`, `computeLoyaltyDiscount`, `isFirstContract` — all still accurately describe current behavior after the recent Green phase (the surcharge-scope fix and the `isFirstQuote` → `isFirstContract` rename). No further renames needed.\n\n**Duplication found (Rule 3 — No Duplication)**:\n`computeRawPolicyPremium` and `computeQuotePremium` both independently computed the item-surcharge total via an inline `items.reduce(...)` expression — the same knowledge (\"total surcharge across items\") was represented twice.\n\n**Current Code Mass (before)** — surcharge-total logic duplicated in two places:\n- `computeRawPolicyPremium` body: bindings 2 (`policyBase`, `itemSurcharges`), invocations 3 (`computeItemsBasePremium`, `reduce`, `computeItemBasePremium`+`computeItemSurchargeRate` inside), loop 1 → mass ≈ 1(binding policyBase)+1(binding itemSurcharges)+2(invocation computeItemsBasePremium)+5(loop reduce)+2(invocation computeItemBasePremium)+2(invocation computeItemSurchargeRate)+1(assignment sum, folded into reduce) ≈ 14\n- `computeQuotePremium`'s `raw` line duplicated the same reduce inline via the call to `computeRawPolicyPremium`, but the *pattern* itself (reduce over items for surcharge) existed as duplicated knowledge, not just duplicated calls.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\nExtracted the shared reduce expression into a named helper `computeItemSurcharges(items)`, and had both `computeRawPolicyPremium` and `computeQuotePremium` call it, removing the duplicated iteration logic and giving the concept (\"sum of all item surcharges\") a single named representation.\n\n**Refactored Code Mass (after)**:\n`