ing Applied** (Rule 4 — Fewest Elements / Rule 2 — Reveals Intent):\n\n`computeReimbursementRate` accepted `Item | undefined` and had an `item &&` guard, but its only caller (`computeDamagePayout`) always passes a concrete, already-validated `Item` (validated by `takeNextInsuredItem`, which throws if missing). The `undefined` branch was dead code that obscured the real precondition.\n\n**Before**:\n```ts\nconst computeReimbursementRate = (item: Item | undefined): number => {\n  if (item && (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return 1;\n};\n```\nMass: bindings 1 (item) + constant 1 (HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD ref is binding, 0 default via `??`... ) — breakdown:\n- Constants: 1 (`0` in `?? 0`), 1 (`1` return) = 2\n- Bindings: 1 (`item`) = 1\n- Invocations: 0 (no calls) = 0\n- Conditionals: 1 (`if` with `&&`) = 4\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\nTotal: **7**\n\n**After**:\n```ts\nconst computeReimbursementRate = (item: Item): number => {\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return 1;\n};\n```\n- Constants: 2 (`0`, `1`)\n- Bindings: 1 (`item`)\n- Invocations: 0\n- Conditionals: 1 (`if`, no `&&`) = 4\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\nTotal: **7**\n\n**Mass Change**: 7 → 7 (no numeric change — `&&` doesn't add mass in this model, but the dead branch and misleading `undefined` type were removed).\n\n**Benefits**: Type signature now accurately reflects the real precondition (item always exists by the time this is called), eliminating a false \"this could be undefined\" signal for future readers, and removing an unreachable code path.\n\n**Tests**: All 10 passing tests remain green; 5 `it.todo()` unaffected."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 10\nRecent Green phase: Added computeCap(policyItems) = computeInsuranceSum(policyItems) * CAP_MULTIPLIER (2), reused from catalog.ts. This is the cap based on unmodified insurance values, ignoring premium modifiers like curse surcharges.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test claim` to verify (vitest requires devDependencies; NODE_ENV=production is set by default in this shell which skips installing them).\n\nRun autonomously, return when done. It's fine to conclude no refactoring needed if minimal -- just document why.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claim.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claim.ts\nPassing tests: 10\nRecent Green phase: Added computeCap(policyItems) = computeInsuranceSum(policyItems) * CAP_MULTIPLIER (2), reused from catalog.ts. This is the cap based on unmodified insurance values, ignoring premium modifiers like curse surcharges.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test claim` to verify (vitest requires devDependencies; NODE_ENV=production is set by default in this shell which skips installing them).\n\nRun autonomously, return when done. It's fine to conclude no refactoring needed if minimal -- just document why."}],"timestamp":1784914778657},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01JuhVo3GFSxyTHPnuCGmYE2","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/src/claim.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01DTzWyUbzVtJyoCaGaoQu8m","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/src/claim.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":325,"output":240,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10321,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784914778682,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-3a822bed-ee6f-459c-8c95-2a473bf98a04","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01JuhVo3GFSxyTHPnuCGmYE2","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { computeInsuranceSum } from \"./catalog.js\";\nimport type { Item } from \"./catalog.js\";\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Incident {\n  cause: string;\n  damages: Damage[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst computeReimbursementRate = (item: Item | undefined): number => {\n  if (item && (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return 1;\n};\n\nconst computeDamagePayout = (item: Item, damage: Damage): number => {\n  const rate = computeReimbursementRate(item);\n  return damage.amount * rate - DEDUCTIBLE;\n};\n\nconst buildItemBucketsByType = (policyItems: Item[]): Map<string, Item[]> => {\n  const bucketsByType = new Map<string, Item[]>();\n  for (const item of policyItems) {\n    const bucket = bucketsByType.get(item.type) ?? [];\n    bucket.push(item);\n    bucketsByType.set(item.type, bucket);\n  }\n  return bucketsByType;\n};\n\nconst takeNextInsuredItem = (bucketsByType: Map<string, Item[]>, itemType: string): Item => {\n  const item = bucketsByType.get(itemType)?.shift();\n  if (!item) {\n    throw new Error(`No insured item of type ${itemType} available for this damage`);\n  }\n  return item;\n};\n\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nexport const computeCap = (policyItems: Item[]): number => computeInsuranceSum(policyItems) * CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nexport const computeClaimPayout = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  incident: Incident,\n  capBeforeClaim: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const bucketsByType = buildItemBucketsByType(policyItems);\n  const payout = incident.damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const item = takeNextInsuredItem(bucketsByType, damage.itemType);\n    return sum + computeDamagePayout(item, damage);\n  }, 0);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: capBeforeClaim - payout };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784914780900},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01DTzWyUbzVtJyoCaGaoQu8m","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computeClaimPayout, computeCap } from \"./claim.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claim - standard reimbursement\", () => {\n  it(\"regular sword (steel, enchantment 3), damage 500 G -- payout 400 G (deductible only)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }];\n    const incident = { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }] };\n    const result = computeClaimPayout(policyItems, incident, 2000);\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"damage to a rune (insurance value 250 G), damage 200 G -- payout 100 G (deductible only, no special clauses)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"rune\" }];\n    const incident = { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }] };\n    const result = computeClaimPayout(policyItems, incident, 500);\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(100);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim - special reimbursement clauses\", () => {\n  it(\"dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -- payout 400 G (50% rule wins over dragon-material, then deductible)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9 }];\n    const incident = { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] };\n    const result = computeClaimPayout(policyItems, incident, 2000);\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G -- payout 700 G (only dragon-material clause: full reimbursement, then deductible)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5 }];\n    const incident = { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }] };\n    const result = computeClaimPayout(policyItems, incident, 2000);\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(700);\n  });\n  it(\"steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G -- payout 400 G (only high-enchantment clause: 50% first, then deductible)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9 }];\n    const incident = { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] };\n    const result = computeClaimPayout(policyItems, incident, 2000);\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"dragon-material sword, exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G -- payout 400 G (high-enchantment threshold clause applies)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 8 }];\n    const incident = { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }] };\n    const result = computeClaimPayout(policyItems, incident, 2000);\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim - deductible per damage event\", () => {\n  it(\"dragon attack damages an insured sword (500 G) and an insured amulet (300 G) -- payout 600 G (100 G deductible applies once per damaged item)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }];\n    const incident = {\n      cause: \"dragon attack\",\n      damages: [\n        { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n        { itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 },\n      ],\n    };\n    const result = computeClaimPayout(policyItems, incident, 3200);\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(600);\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim - multiple items of the same type\", () => {\n  it(\"policy covers two swords, damages array has two sword entries -- each entry is a separate damage with its own deductible\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"sword\" }];\n    const incident = {\n      cause: \"dragon attack\",\n      damages: [\n        { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n        { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n      ],\n    };\n    const result = computeClaimPayout(policyItems, incident, 4000);\n    expect(result.payout).toBe(800);\n  });\n  it(\"damages array has more entries of a type than the policy covers -- throws an error\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\" }];\n    const incident = {\n      cause: \"dragon attack\",\n      damages: [\n        { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n        { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(() => computeClaimPayout(policyItems, incident, 2000)).toThrow();\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim - cap exhaustion\", () => {\n  it(\"cursed sword (insurance value 1000 G) -- cap is 2000 G, based on unmodified insurance value\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", cursed: true }];\n    expect(computeCap(policyItems)).toBe(2000);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"sword insured (cap 2000 G); first claim of 1500 G -- payout 1400 G, remaining cap 600 G\");\n  it.todo(\"sword insured (cap 2000 G); second successive claim of 1500 G after first -- payout 600 G, remaining cap 0 G\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Claim - error cases\", () => {\n  it.todo(\"claim references a damage entry whose item is not part of the policy -- throws an error\");\n  it.todo(\"claim references a damage entry with an unknown item type -- throws an error\");\n  it.todo(\"claim contains a damage entry with amount -200 -- throws an error\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784914780900},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01BECQSdmhV7vWpiAHK57QhF","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/src/catalog.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3494,"output":148,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13398,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784914780900,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-585e4b19-5948-4851-b63a-1b26de16dec5","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01BECQSdmhV7vWpiAHK57QhF","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Item {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nconst ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PREMIUM = 60;\n\nconst computeTypePremium = (type: string, count: number): number => {\n  if (!(type in ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM)) {\n    throw new Error(`Unknown item type: ${type}`);\n  }\n  return count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PREMIUM : count * ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM[type];\n};\n\nexport const computeItemBasePremium = (item: Item): number => computeTypePremium(item.type, 1);\n\nexport const computeItemsBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const countsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const { type } of items) {\n    countsByType.set(type, (countsByType.get(type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  return [...countsByType].reduce(\n    (total, [type, count]) => total + computeTypePremium(type, count),\n    0\n  );\n};\n\nconst ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  rune: 250,\n};\n\nexport const computeInsuranceSum = (items: Item[]): number =>\n  items.reduce((sum, { type }) => sum + ITEM_INSURANCE_VALUE[type], 0);\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784914783466},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_014zN5sENmENQ4p9rxigAvAX","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && NODE_ENV=development pnpm test claim 2>&1 | tail -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":4189,"output":153,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14098,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784914783466,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-f09cf1d8-7f9e-4670-90a5-a66e841c3892","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_014zN5sENmENQ4p9rxigAvAX","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n> vitest run claim\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n\n ✓ src/claim.spec.ts  (15 tests | 5 skipped) 3ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  10 passed | 5 todo (15)\n   Start at  17:39:45\n   Duration  156ms (transform 29ms, setup 0ms, collect 29ms, tests 3ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784914785929},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01J3hdnyF9YwtCeQe5novqFP","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && grep -n \"\" src/claim.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":4300,"output":1467,"cacheRead":10079,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15846,"cost":{