rpose is \"cap = insurance sum × multiplier, based on unmodified insurance values, ignoring premium modifiers.\" The name is short but the test/comment context makes intent clear via the `CAP_MULTIPLIER` constant and JSDoc-style call chain. Kept as-is — renaming to something like `computeUnmodifiedInsuranceCap` would be more precise but adds verbosity without much clarity gain given the surrounding constant name and single call site. **Decision: keep name.**\n- `computeReimbursementRate`, `computeDamagePayout`, `buildItemBucketsByType`, `takeNextInsuredItem`, `computeClaimPayout`: all still accurately describe behavior after this Green phase — the cap logic didn't change their responsibilities. No renames needed.\n\n**Refactoring Applied** (Rule 4 — Fewest Elements / Rule 2 — Reveals Intent):\n\n`computeReimbursementRate` accepted `Item | undefined` and had an `item &&` guard, but its only caller (`computeDamagePayout`) always passes a concrete, already-validated `Item` (validated by `takeNextInsuredItem`, which throws if missing). The `undefined` branch was dead code that obscured the real precondition.\n\n**Before**:\n```ts\nconst computeReimbursementRate = (item: Item | undefined): number => {\n  if (item && (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return 1;\n};\n```\nMass: bindings 1 (item) + constant 1 (HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD ref is binding, 0 default via `??`... ) — breakdown:\n- Constants: 1 (`0` in `?? 0`), 1 (`1` return) = 2\n- Bindings: 1 (`item`) = 1\n- Invocations: 0 (no calls) = 0\n- Conditionals: 1 (`if` with `&&`) = 4\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\nTotal: **7**\n\n**After**:\n```ts\nconst computeReimbursementRate = (item: Item): number => {\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return 1;\n};\n```\n- Constants: 2 (`0`, `1`)\n- Bindings: 1 (`item`)\n- Invocations: 0\n- Conditionals: 1 (`if`, no `&&`) = 4\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0\nTotal: **7**\n\n**Mass Change**: 7 → 7 (no numeric change — `&&` doesn't add mass in this model, but the dead branch and misleading `undefined` type were removed).\n\n**Benefits**: Type signature now accurately reflects the real precondition (item always exists by the time this is called), eliminating a false \"this could be undefined\" signal for future readers, and removing an unreachable code path.\n\n**Tests**: All 10 passing tests remain green; 5 `it.todo()` unaffected."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":6580,"output":1139,"cacheRead":10079,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17798,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784914861455,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-cb23af1c-ae0d-4ce3-8678-077182eeb43c","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":36175,"output":9057,"cacheRead":79663,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":17798,"turns":8},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784914873030},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01ABegfCC6VSi5Apx9ppffJw","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && cat src/claim.ts && NODE_ENV=development pnpm test claim 2>&1 | tail -10"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":2447,"output":148,"cacheRead":179979,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":182574,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784914873035,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-88b84300-ab85-4115-8a5b-f335ba955510","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01ABegfCC6VSi5Apx9ppffJw","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { computeInsuranceSum } from \"./catalog.js\";\nimport type { Item } from \"./catalog.js\";\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Incident {\n  cause: string;\n  damages: Damage[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst computeReimbursementRate = (item: Item): number => {\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return 1;\n};\n\nconst computeDamagePayout = (item: Item, damage: Damage): number => {\n  const rate = computeReimbursementRate(item);\n  return damage.amount * rate - DEDUCTIBLE;\n};\n\nconst buildItemBucketsByType = (policyItems: Item[]): Map<string, Item[]> => {\n  const bucketsByType = new Map<string, Item[]>();\n  for (const item of policyItems) {\n    const bucket = bucketsByType.get(item.type) ?? [];\n    bucket.push(item);\n    bucketsByType.set(item.type, bucket);\n  }\n  return bucketsByType;\n};\n\nconst takeNextInsuredItem = (bucketsByType: Map<string, Item[]>, itemType: string): Item => {\n  const item = bucketsByType.get(itemType)?.shift();\n  if (!item) {\n    throw new Error(`No insured item of type ${itemType} available for this damage`);\n  }\n  return item;\n};\n\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nexport const computeCap = (policyItems: Item[]): number => computeInsuranceSum(policyItems) * CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nexport const computeClaimPayout = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  incident: Incident,\n  capBeforeClaim: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const bucketsByType = buildItemBucketsByType(policyItems);\n  const payout = incident.damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const item = takeNextInsuredItem(bucketsByType, damage.itemType);\n    return sum + computeDamagePayout(item, damage);\n  }, 0);\n  return { payout, remainin