mPayout(policy.items, step.incident, policy.remainingCap);\n  policy.remainingCap = remainingCap;\n  return { payout, remainingCap };\n});\n```\n- Bindings: index, premium, policy, payout, remainingCap = 5\n- Invocations: map, computeQuotePremium, set, computeCap, getPolicyOrThrow, computeClaimPayout = 6 → mass 12\n- Conditionals: 1 (if) = 4\n- Loops: 1 (map) = 5\n- Assignments: 1 (policy.remainingCap = remainingCap) = 6\n- Constants: true = 1\n\nTotal Mass: 5 + 12 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 1 = **33**\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```\nconst handleQuoteStep = (step: QuoteStep, stepIndex: number): QuoteResult => {\n  const premium = computeQuotePremium(input.customer, step.items, true);\n  policiesByStepIndex.set(stepIndex, { items: step.items, remainingCap: computeCap(step.items) });\n  return { premium };\n};\n\nconst handleClaimStep = (step: ClaimStep): ClaimStepResult => {\n  const policy = getPolicyOrThrow(policiesByStepIndex, step.policy);\n  const { payout, remainingCap } = computeClaimPayout(policy.items, step.incident, policy.remainingCap);\n  policy.remainingCap = remainingCap;\n  return { payout, remainingCap };\n};\n\nconst results: StepResult[] = input.steps.map((step, index) =>\n  step.op === \"quote\" ? handleQuoteStep(step, index) : handleClaimStep(step)\n);\n```\n- Bindings: stepIndex, premium, policy, payout, remainingCap, index = 6\n- Invocations: computeQuotePremium, set, computeCap, getPolicyOrThrow, computeClaimPayout, map, handleQuoteStep, handleClaimStep = 8 → mass 16\n- Conditionals: 1 (ternary) = 4\n- Loops: 1 (map) = 5\n- Assignments: 1 = 6\n- Constants: true = 1\n\nTotal Mass: 6 + 16 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 1 = **38**\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Extracted the two branches of the `map` callback into named functions `handleQuoteStep` / `handleClaimStep`, replacing the `if` block with a single ternary expression that reads as a direct dispatch on `step.op`.\n- Mass increased slightly (33 → 38, delta +5) due to two extra function-invocation nodes, but Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP here: the top-level `map` body is now a one-line, self-documenting dispatch, and each step-handling concern is isolated and independently readable/testable in code review.\n\n**Rule Evaluation Summary**:\n- Rule 1 (Tests Pass): All 6 scenario tests and the full 49-test suite stay green.\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent): Improved — the branching logic per step type is now named and separated from the iteration mechanics.\n- Rule 3 (No Duplication): No duplication found; not applicable.\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): Slightly more elements (two extra functions), accepted as a deliberate clarity trade-off per Rule 2 priority over APP mass.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `handleQuoteStep`/`handleClaimStep` helpers from the inline `if` branch in `runScenario`, replacing it with a ternary dispatch.\n**Mass Change**: 33 -> 38 (+5, accepted for clarity per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 49 passing (6/6 in scenario.spec.ts)"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/scenario.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/scenario.ts\nPassing tests: 6 (all scenario tests complete)\nRecent Green phase: All 6 scenario.spec.ts tests now pass without further changes needed (they were satisfied by the existing implementation from the previous cycle). runScenario processes quote/claim steps sequentially, tracking policies (items + remainingCap) in a Map keyed by step index, using getPolicyOrThrow for claim-step lookups.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test scenario` to verify (vitest requires devDependencies; NODE_ENV=production is set by default in this shell which skips installing them).\n\nSince scenario.spec.ts is now fully implemented (no more it.todo), feel free to look at the whole file holistically for any final cleanup, but keep changes conservative and don't add behavior beyond what tests demand.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/scenario.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/scenario.ts\nPassing tests: 6 (all scenario tests complete)\nRecent Green phase: All 6 scenario.spec.ts tests now pass without further changes needed (they were satisfied by the existing implementation from the previous cycle). runScenario processes quote/claim steps sequentially, tracking policies (items + remainingCap) in a Map keyed by step index, using getPolicyOrThrow for claim-step lookups.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green. Run `NODE_ENV=development pnpm test scenario` to verify (vitest requires devDependencies; NODE_ENV=production is set by default in this shell which skips installing them).\n\nSince scenario.spec.ts is now fully implemented (no more it.todo), feel free to look at the whole file holistically for any final cleanup, but keep changes conservative and don't add behavior beyond what tests demand.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784915602026},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01TTFqmobpLcKEnumSWgusdT","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/scenario.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_0177tv29RNSSukCg6joX2q4r","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/scenario.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":407,"output":122,"cacheRead":9756,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10285,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784915602046,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-8bddd653-ec37-4abb-b5ad-f31203a18f82","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01TTFqmobpLcKEnumSWgusdT","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { Item } from \"./catalog.js\";\nimport { computeQuotePremium } from \"./quote.js\";\nimport { computeCap, computeClaimPayout, type Incident } from \"./claim.js\";\n\nexport interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: Incident;\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface ScenarioInput {\n  customer: Customer;\n  steps: Step[];\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStepResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport type StepResult = QuoteResult | ClaimStepResult;\n\nexport interface ScenarioOutput {\n  results: StepResult[];\n}\n\ninterface Policy {\n  items: Item[];\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst getPolicyOrThrow = (policiesByStepIndex: Map<number, Policy>, stepIndex: number): Policy => {\n  const policy = policiesByStepIndex.get(stepIndex);\n  if (!policy) {\n    throw new Error(`No policy found at step index ${stepIndex}`);\n  }\n  return policy;\n};\n\nexport const runScenario = (input: ScenarioInput): ScenarioOutput => {\n  const policiesByStepIndex = new Map<number, Policy>();\n  const results: StepResult[] = input.steps.map((step, index) => {\n    if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n      const premium = computeQuotePremium(input.customer, step.items, true);\n      policiesByStepIndex.set(index, { items: step.items, remainingCap: computeCap(step.items) });\n      return { premium };\n    }\n    const policy = getPolicyOrThrow(policiesByStepIndex, step.policy);\n    const { payout, remainingCap } = computeClaimPayout(policy.items, step.incident, policy.remainingCap);\n    policy.remainingCap = remainingCap;\n    return { payout, remainingCap };\n  });\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784915604099},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_0177tv29RNSSukCg6joX2q4r","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./scenario.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Scenario runner - schema example\", () => {\n  it(\"schema example scenario (amulet quote then claim) -- produces premium and payout/remainingCap results\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 5 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\",\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 200 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    const output = runScenario(scenario);\n    expect(output.results).toHaveLength(2);\n    expect(output.results[0]).toHaveProperty(\"premium\");\n    expect(output.results[1]).toHaveProperty(\"payout\");\n    expect(output.results[1]).toHaveProperty(\"remainingCap\");\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Scenario runner - multi-step scenarios\", () => {\n  it(\"quote step followed by claim step referencing policy index 0 -- payout uses that policy's insurance sum for the cap\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    const output = runScenario(scenario);\n    expect(output.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 400, remainingCap: 1600 });\n  });\n  it(\"two successive claim steps against the same policy -- second claim's remaining cap reflects the first claim's payout\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }] },\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    const output = runScenario(scenario);\n    expect(output.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 1400, remainingCap: 600 });\n    expect(output.results[2]).toEqual({ payout: 600, remainingCap: 0 });\n  });\n});\n\ndescribe(\"Scenario runner - error cases surface as thrown errors\", () => {\n  it(\"a quote step with an unknown item type -- throws an error\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"broomstick\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(() => runScenario(scenario)).toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"a claim step referencing a damage item not part of the policy -- throws an error\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(() => runScenario(scenario)).toThrow();\n  });\n  it(\"a claim step with a negative damage amount -- throws an error\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\", items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\",\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: -200 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(() => runScenario(scenario)).toThrow();\n  });\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784915604099},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01WtAULMpgmK8w1y5UqpSyoS","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && NODE_ENV=development pnpm test scenario 2>&1 | tail -40"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01QCiXgkKDD8oS2fwSLept2n","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claim.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":2294,"output":226,"cacheRead":10161,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12681,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784915604100,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-f0e9dd10-3f06-4e33-988b-93934e355642","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01WtAULMpgmK8w1y5UqpSyoS","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n> vitest run scenario\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5\n\n ✓ src/scenario.spec.ts  (6 tests) 4ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  6 passed (6)\n   Start at  17:53:27\n   Duration  163ms (transform 34ms, setup 0ms, collect 35ms, tests 4ms, environment 0ms, prepare 41ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784915607916},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01QCiXgkKDD8oS2fwSLept2n","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { computeInsuranceSum, type Item } from \"./catalog.js\";\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Incident {\n  cause: string;\n  damages: Damage[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\n\nconst computeReimbursementRate = (item: Item): number => {\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD) {\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return 1;\n};\n\nconst computeDamagePayout = (item: Item, damage: Damage): number => {\n  if (damage.amount < 0) {\n    throw new Error(`Damage amount cannot be negative: ${damage.amount}`);\n  }\n  const rate = computeReimbursementRate(item);\n  return damage.amount * rate - DEDUCTIBLE;\n};\n\nconst buildItemBucketsByType = (policyItems: Item[]): Map<string, Item[]> => {\n  const bucketsByType = new Map<string, Item[]>();\n  for (const item of policyItems) {\n    const bucket = bucketsByType.get(item.type) ?? [];\n    bucket.push(item);\n    bucketsByType.set(item.type, bucket);\n  }\n  return bucketsByType;\n};\n\nconst takeNextInsuredItem = (bucketsByType: Map<string, Item[]>, itemType: string): Item => {\n  const item = bucketsByType.get(itemType)?.shift();\n  if (!item) {\n    throw new Error(`No insured item of type ${itemType} available for this damage`);\n  }\n  return item;\n};\n\nconst CAP_MULTIPLIER = 2;\n\nexport const computeCap = (policyItems: Item[]): number => computeInsuranceSum(policyItems) * CAP_MULTIPLIER;\n\nconst computeDesiredPayout = (policyItems: Item[], damages: Damage[]): number => {\n  const bucketsByType = buildItemBucketsByType(policyItems);\n  return damages.reduce((sum, damage) => {\n    const item = takeNextInsuredItem(bucketsByType, damage.itemType);\n    return sum + computeDamagePayout(item, damage);\n  }, 0);\n};\n\nexport const computeClaimPayout = (\n  policyItems: Item[],\n  incident: Incident,\n  capBeforeClaim: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const desiredPayout = computeDesiredPayout(policyItems, incident.damages);\n  const payout = Math.min(desiredPayout, capBeforeClaim);\n  return { payout, remainingCap: capBeforeClaim - payout };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784915607916},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01TXZv1niEDsdXjDaqNbeW3m","name":"bash","arguments":{"com