:"text","text":"All 49 tests pass, no regressions.\n\n## Refactoring Report\n\n**Naming Evaluation**:\n- Current names: `runScenario`, `getPolicyOrThrow`, `handleQuoteStep` (new), `handleClaimStep` (new)\n- `runScenario` clearly reveals intent: it runs a scenario of quote/claim steps. Purpose hasn't changed across the 6 tests — no rename needed.\n- `getPolicyOrThrow` also clearly states its behavior (lookup + throw). Kept as-is.\n\nDecision: Keep existing names; introduce two new, clearly-named helpers (`handleQuoteStep`, `handleClaimStep`) extracted from the inline `if` branch inside the map callback.\n\n**Current Code Mass** (body of `runScenario`, inline branching form):\n```\nconst results: StepResult[] = input.steps.map((step, index) => {\n  if (step.op === \"quote\") {\n    const premium = computeQuotePremium(input.customer, step.items, true);\n    policiesByStepIndex.set(index, { items: step.items, remainingCap: computeCap(step.items) });\n    return { premium };\n  }\n  const policy = getPolicyOrThrow(policiesByStepIndex, step.policy);\n  const { payout, remainingCap } = computeClaimPayout(policy.items, step.incident, policy.remainingCap);\n  policy.remainingCap = remainingCap;\n  return { payout, remainingCap };\n});\n```\n- Bindings: index, premium, policy, payout, remainingCap = 5\n- Invocations: map, computeQuotePremium, set, computeCap, getPolicyOrThrow, computeClaimPayout = 6 → mass 12\n- Conditionals: 1 (if) = 4\n- Loops: 1 (map) = 5\n- Assignments: 1 (policy.remainingCap = remainingCap) = 6\n- Constants: true = 1\n\nTotal Mass: 5 + 12 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 1 = **33**\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```\nconst handleQuoteStep = (step: QuoteStep, stepIndex: number): QuoteResult => {\n  const premium = computeQuotePremium(input.customer, step.items, true);\n  policiesByStepIndex.set(stepIndex, { items: step.items, remainingCap: computeCap(step.items) });\n  return { premium };\n};\n\nconst handleClaimStep = (step: ClaimStep): ClaimStepResult => {\n  const policy = getPolicyOrThrow(policiesByStepIndex, step.policy);\n  const { payout, remainingCap } = computeClaimPayout(policy.items, step.incident, policy.remainingCap);\n  policy.remainingCap = remainingCap;\n  return { payout, remainingCap };\n};\n\nconst results: StepResult[] = input.steps.map((step, index) =>\n  step.op === \"quote\" ? handleQuoteStep(step, index) : handleClaimStep(step)\n);\n```\n- Bindings: stepIndex, premium, policy, payout, remainingCap, index = 6\n- Invocations: computeQuotePremium, set, computeCap, getPolicyOrThrow, computeClaimPayout, map, handleQuoteStep, handleClaimStep = 8 → mass 16\n- Conditionals: 1 (ternary) = 4\n- Loops: 1 (map) = 5\n- Assignments: 1 = 6\n- Constants: true = 1\n\nTotal Mass: 6 + 16 + 4 + 5 + 6 + 1 = **38**\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Extracted the two branches of the `map` callback into named functions `handleQuoteStep` / `handleClaimStep`, replacing the `if` block with a single ternary expression that reads as a direct dispatch on `step.op`.\n- Mass increased slightly (33 → 38, delta +5) due to two extra function-invocation nodes, but Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP here: the top-level `map` body is now a one-line, self-documenting dispatch, and each step-handling concern is isolated and independently readable/testable in code review.\n\n**Rule Evaluation Summary**:\n- Rule 1 (Tests Pass): All 6 scenario tests and the full 49-test suite stay green.\n- Rule 2 (Reveals Intent): Improved — the branching logic per step type is now named and separated from the iteration mechanics.\n- Rule 3 (No Duplication): No duplication found; not applicable.\n- Rule 4 (Fewest Elements): Slightly more elements (two extra functions), accepted as a deliberate clarity trade-off per Rule 2 priority over APP mass.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Extracted `handleQuoteStep`/`handleClaimStep` helpers from the inline `if` branch in `runScenario`, replacing it with a ternary dispatch.\n**Mass Change**: 33 -> 38 (+5, accepted for clarity per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 49 passing (6/6 in scenario.spec.ts)"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":6240,"output":1732,"cacheRead":10161,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":18133,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784915707543,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-b3484296-efe9-4f87-8a6b-f3ca833ea586","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":38584,"output":12428,"cacheRead":60156,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":18133,"turns":7},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784915722559},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01VJK2V57M9GKxKsnvCZfSFD","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_16-23-48_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5 && cat src/scenario.ts && NODE_ENV=development pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -20"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":2731,"output":147,"cacheRead":210685,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":213563,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784915722566,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-7d6894bc-73b3-4e19-b441-6cc32d5b5710","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01VJK2V57M9GKxKsnvCZfSFD","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { Item } from \"./catalog.js\";\nimport { computeQuotePremium } from \"./quote.js\";\nimport { computeCap, computeClaimPayout, type Incident } from \"./claim.js\";\n\nexport interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: Item[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: Incident;\n}\n\nexport type Step =